Date: Sat, 19 Sep 2026 03:28:32 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 8/8] docs, streamaggr: document sum_samples_total and
 reset_marker_on_stale

Both were wired through the code but appeared nowhere in the docs, so
anyone writing an aggregation config from the documentation had no way to
know they exist.

Adds the output section for sum_samples_total, saying what it is for
(inputs that already are increments), how it differs from total (no state
per input series, so memory does not follow the number of inputs merged
into one output, and no baseline sample to drop after a restart) and that
it wants reset_marker_on_stale alongside. Adds reset_marker_on_stale to
the aggregation config options, saying which outputs it applies to and
what goes wrong without it.

Also adds sum_samples_total to the outputs BenchmarkAggregatorsPush
covers, so it has the same regression guard as the rest. On that
benchmark it is about 3% faster than total and allocates half as much
(34 vs 71 allocations per operation at a settled benchtime).
